      "message": "This is good; however, the description still doesn\u0027t match the issue.\nAlso, the documentation details on how to disable the cache can be found in the original change\nrather than copying and pasting it all here.\n\n```suggestion\n* [Issue 561066231](https://issues.gerritcodereview.com/issues/561066231):\n  The `oauth_tokens` cache is now encrypted in core: `OAuthTokenCache` and its\n  H2 persistence has been part of Gerrit core since the feature was introduced, so\n  encrypting the stored tokens is a core data-protection concern.\n\n  \u003e **NOTE**: Setting `cache.oauth_tokens.memoryLimit \u003d 0` now fully disables OAuth token\n  \u003e storage, so tokens are no longer written to the persistent H2 cache even when\n  \u003e `diskLimit` is positive. See [Change 630421](https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/gerrit/+/630421)\n  \u003e for more details.\n```",
